-- title:
--   Cyclic cyclotomic extensions of prescribed p-power degree
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, let $p$ be a prime number and let $a$ be a natural number. The assertion is that there exist a natural number $k$ and an intermediate field $L$ of the extension $K \subseteq \mathrm{CyclotomicField}(p^k, K)$, the cyclotomic extension of $K$ generated by the $p^k$-th roots of unity, such that: $L$ is Galois over $K$; the group $L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L$ of $K$-algebra automorphisms of $L$ is cyclic; and the $K$-dimension of $L$, as a $K$-module, equals $p^a$. Thus inside some cyclotomic tower $K(\zeta_{p^k})/K$ one finds a cyclic Galois subextension whose degree over $K$ is exactly $p^a$, not merely divisible by or bounded below by $p^a$. No condition relating $p$ to $K$ is imposed, and the exponent $k$ is produced by the statement rather than prescribed; the degenerate case $a = 0$ is included, where $L = K$ is permitted.
--
--   This is the place-free form of the auxiliary cyclic-extension lemma ("Artin's lemma") used in the Artin–Tate treatment of the idèle class group as a class formation, where the fundamental class of a suitable cyclic cyclotomic layer is inflated to produce cohomology classes of prescribed order. In this development it feeds the construction of an element of $H^2$ of the correct order for $p$-groups, via [`M4aHerbrand.exists_natCard_H2_eq_card_and_span_eq_top_ideleClassGroup_of_isPGroup`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.exists_natCard_H2_eq_card_and_span_eq_top_ideleClassGroup_of_isPGroup).
-- source:
